From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx678: RZ/V2N IMX678 RAW12 camera support

Roll up SolidRun's IMX678 RZ/V2N camera enablement on top of the will127534
IMX678 driver already present in the pinned kernel (KERNEL_REV):

 - imx678.c: reference-register tuning (WINMODE crop, DATARATE_SEL, PIX
   window, HMAX/VMAX, BLKLEVEL), reworked link-frequency/pixel-rate handling
   (IMX678_LINK_FREQ_594MHZ), crop-window registers, and the set_pad_format
   TRY-format fix.
 - rzg2l-cru: add the standard 12-bit Bayer CRU output formats (RG12/BG12/...)
   and RZ/V2N demosaic gating.

Generated from the SolidRun linux-stable rz-6.1-cip43 development head; applies
on the pinned KERNEL_REV. The RAW12 line-truncation fix is a separate patch.

Signed-off-by: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
